From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Maestro: release node parameter tables in ~CMovieSystem()

CMovieSystem::DoNodeStaticInitialisation() and the node constructors
fill file-scope AZStd tables (the post-FX descriptions and the scene,
layer, screen fader, comment and shadow setup parameter lists) that
nothing empties. In a monolithic build their destructors run from the
exit handlers after the SystemAllocator's environment variable is
destroyed, so every deallocation calls a pure virtual on the dead
allocator and an exported release game aborts on quit with "pure
virtual method called" (o3de-development 2610.0-126, Fedora 44/45 and
CentOS Stream 10, 2026-10-22).

Release the tables from ~CMovieSystem(), which runs in
CSystem::ShutDown() while the allocators are still alive, and reset the
init flags so a later CMovieSystem fills them again. The vectors are
swapped with empty ones because clear() keeps their buffers.

diff --git a/Gems/Maestro/Code/Source/Cinematics/AnimPostFXNode.cpp b/Gems/Maestro/Code/Source/Cinematics/AnimPostFXNode.cpp
index fa5f663714..327c7cea8e 100644
--- a/Gems/Maestro/Code/Source/Cinematics/AnimPostFXNode.cpp
+++ b/Gems/Maestro/Code/Source/Cinematics/AnimPostFXNode.cpp
@@ -212,6 +212,12 @@ namespace Maestro
         }
     }
 
+    void CAnimPostFXNode::Shutdown()
+    {
+        s_initialized = false;
+        s_fxNodeDescriptions.clear();
+    }
+
     /*static*/ CFXNodeDescription* CAnimPostFXNode::GetFXNodeDescription(AnimNodeType nodeType)
     {
         CFXNodeDescription* retDescription = nullptr;
diff --git a/Gems/Maestro/Code/Source/Cinematics/AnimPostFXNode.h b/Gems/Maestro/Code/Source/Cinematics/AnimPostFXNode.h
